<%- include('../partials/admin-top', { title }) %>

<h1>AI settings</h1>
<p class="sub">Point the bot at your self-hosted Llama (Ollama) or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint.</p>

<% if (testResult) { %>
<div class="flash <%= testResult.ok ? 'flash-ok' : 'flash-err' %>"><%= testResult.ok ? '✅ ' : '❌ ' %><%= testResult.detail %></div>
<% } %>

<form method="post" action="/admin/ai">
  <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="checkline">
      <input type="checkbox" id="enabled" name="enabled" value="1" <%= s.enabled ? 'checked' : '' %>>
      <label for="enabled">AI answering enabled (off = keyword matching only, answers sent verbatim)</label>
    </div>

    <label for="baseUrl">Endpoint base URL (OpenAI-compatible)</label>
    <input id="baseUrl" name="baseUrl" type="url" value="<%= s.baseUrl %>" placeholder="http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1" required>
    <p class="hint">Two things catch people out, and they fail one after the other rather than together: a self-hosted Ollama serves <strong>plain <code>http://</code></strong> (an <code>https://</code> address gives <code>ERR_SSL_WRONG_VERSION_NUMBER</code>), and the URL must <strong>end in <code>/v1</code></strong> or every request 404s. An Ollama server on its own Pelican egg looks like <code>http://your-node.example.com:25569/v1</code>.</p>
    <p class="hint">⚠ On Pelican, <code>127.0.0.1</code> is the container itself — for Ollama on the same node use the Docker gateway <code>http://172.17.0.1:11434/v1</code> or the node's LAN IP, and run Ollama with <code>OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0</code>. Groq cloud: <code>https://api.groq.com/openai/v1</code>.</p>

    <div class="row">
      <div>
        <label for="model">Model name</label>
        <input id="model" name="model" type="text" value="<%= s.model %>" placeholder="llama3.1" required>
        <p class="hint">CPU-only node? Prefer <code>llama3.1:8b</code> or <code>qwen2.5:7b</code> — they reuse the cached prompt between messages. Avoid <code>gemma3</code> on CPU: it re-reads the whole prompt on every message (~1 min per reply).</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="apiKey">API key (leave empty for local Ollama)</label>
        <input id="apiKey" name="apiKey" type="password" value="<%= s.apiKey %>" autocomplete="off">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
      <div>
        <label for="maxTokens">Max reply tokens</label>
        <input id="maxTokens" name="maxTokens" type="number" min="50" max="4000" value="<%= s.maxTokens %>">
        <p class="hint">Roughly 4 characters a token, so 500 is about 350 words — enough for a step-by-step install guide. Set it too low and guides get cut off mid-instruction, which the customer notices; set it very high and a slow node spends longer on every answer.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="temperature">Temperature (0 = factual, 1 = creative)</label>
        <input id="temperature" name="temperature" type="number" step="0.1" min="0" max="2" value="<%= s.temperature %>">
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="timeoutSeconds">Answer timeout (seconds)</label>
        <input id="timeoutSeconds" name="timeoutSeconds" type="number" min="10" max="600" value="<%= s.timeoutSeconds %>">
        <p class="hint">How long a customer may wait. Answers stream in, so hitting this sends whatever the model has finished saying rather than failing — and a node that goes silent mid-answer is dropped straight away. If answers arrive cut short, the node is too slow for the prompt: use a smaller model or trim your knowledge and guides. Raising this only makes people wait longer.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="maxConcurrent">Parallel AI answers (1 for CPU Ollama)</label>
        <input id="maxConcurrent" name="maxConcurrent" type="number" min="1" max="8" value="<%= s.maxConcurrent %>">
        <p class="hint">Extra questions wait in line automatically; when the line is full the bot replies with the "busy" message from Bot settings.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="dailyBudget">Daily AI call budget (0 = unlimited)</label>
        <input id="dailyBudget" name="dailyBudget" type="number" min="0" max="100000" value="<%= s.dailyBudget %>">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Understanding questions</h2>
    <p class="sub">With this on, the AI writes every answer and your knowledge entries become the facts it answers <em>from</em> — instead of a keyword match firing a canned entry at a question it only looked like. If the embedding model isn't available the bot falls back to keyword matching automatically, so nothing breaks.</p>
    <div class="checkline">
      <input type="checkbox" id="embedEnabled" name="embedEnabled" value="1" <%= s.embedEnabled ? 'checked' : '' %>>
      <label for="embedEnabled">Match questions by meaning (recommended)</label>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div>
        <label for="embedModel">Embedding model</label>
        <input id="embedModel" name="embedModel" type="text" maxlength="100" value="<%= s.embedModel %>">
        <p class="hint">Pull it once on your node: <code>ollama pull nomic-embed-text</code>. It's small and fast even on CPU — an embedding is one pass over the question, not a generated answer.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="retrieveCount">Knowledge entries given to the model per question</label>
        <input id="retrieveCount" name="retrieveCount" type="number" min="1" max="20" value="<%= s.retrieveCount %>">
        <p class="hint">More context costs more reading time before the first word comes back.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Answer reuse</h2>
    <p class="sub">The same questions get asked forever in a support group. When a new question means essentially the same thing as one already answered, the stored answer is sent instantly instead of the node spending minutes rewriting it. A 👎 removes that answer, and editing any knowledge entry or guide retires every answer written before the edit.</p>
    <div class="checkline">
      <input type="checkbox" id="cacheEnabled" name="cacheEnabled" value="1" <%= s.cacheEnabled ? 'checked' : '' %>>
      <label for="cacheEnabled">Reuse answers for repeat questions (recommended)</label>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div>
        <label for="cacheThreshold">How alike two questions must be (0.5–1)</label>
        <input id="cacheThreshold" name="cacheThreshold" type="number" step="0.01" min="0.5" max="1" value="<%= s.cacheThreshold %>">
        <p class="hint">0.95 is strict — near-identical wording only. Lower it to reuse more and risk answering a question that was merely similar.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p><button type="submit">Save AI settings</button></p>
</form>

<form method="post" action="/admin/ai/test">
  <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
  <button type="submit" class="btn-ghost">Test connection</button>
</form>

<%- include('../partials/admin-bottom') %>
